# EXAMPLE ONLY. GitHub reads CODEOWNERS only from .github/CODEOWNERS (or the repository root or docs/);
# this file is deliberately named .example so it has no effect until real teams exist.
# Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace the placeholders with real GitHub teams or users.
# Rules follow docs/ci-cd-pipeline.md Section 5: two reviewers for security-relevant paths (set the
# required approval count in branch protection; CODEOWNERS only selects who must review).

# Default
*                         @ORG/security-engineers

# Policy, migrations, deployment, controls, pipeline, requirements: security architect plus delivery lead
/policy/                  @ORG/security-architects @ORG/delivery-leads
/db/migrations/           @ORG/security-architects @ORG/delivery-leads
/deploy/                  @ORG/security-architects @ORG/platform-operators
/controls/                @ORG/security-architects @ORG/compliance
/.github/                 @ORG/security-architects @ORG/delivery-leads
/Plan/functional-spec.md  @ORG/product-owners @ORG/security-architects
/compliance/              @ORG/compliance @ORG/security-architects
